NetPrint Privacy Policy

Last updated: November 4, 2026  
Operator: SunnyStark  
Contact: ycfiggy@gmail.com

## 1. Files, photos and scans
When you select files or photos or use the camera to scan, NetPrint processes that content to import, preview, save and print it. Imported files, scans and file records are stored primarily on your device. We currently provide no operator-hosted file cloud sync and do not intentionally upload your documents, photos or scans for advertising. Apple device backups may include app data according to your system settings and Apple’s policies.

## 2. Printers and local network
With system permission, the app accesses your local network to discover compatible printers and process their names, network addresses, capabilities and your print settings. When you print, selected content is sent through the system printing service to your chosen printer. Choose trusted devices and networks and protect printed pages.

## 3. Browsing and search
Web printing uses an embedded browser. The default website may be Yahoo! JAPAN, Baidu or Google, depending on your system region. Websites and their providers may receive your IP address, browser information, searches, cookies and information you submit. Their privacy policies govern their processing, including cookies, login storage, ads and tracking. Some pages may use unencrypted HTTP; avoid entering passwords, payment details or other sensitive information on those pages.

## 4. Purchases
Apple App Store and StoreKit process purchases. NetPrint reads product identifiers, transaction identifiers, subscription expiry and purchase status to verify and restore benefits. We do not receive your full card details, Apple Account password or payment password. Apple handles payment and refunds under its policies.

## 5. Advertising
The free version uses Google AdMob (Google Mobile Ads SDK) and Google’s User Messaging Platform for applicable advertising privacy choices. Depending on SDK version, region, permissions and choices, Google may process IP addresses, device or advertising identifiers, ad impressions and interactions, diagnostics and performance information, and approximate location inferred from IP addresses. Purposes include ad delivery, measurement, fraud prevention and service maintenance.
Where Apple-defined cross-app or website tracking is involved, we obtain authorization as required. Refusing tracking does not prevent basic app use and does not mean all ad-related processing stops. With active VIP or ad-removal benefits, NetPrint stops actively requesting and showing its own ads; third-party websites you visit may still contain ads or tracking.
Google privacy: https://policies.google.com/privacy  
Google advertising: https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads

## 6. Permissions
Camera access supports scanning; photo access supports importing selected images; local network access supports printer discovery and connection. Tracking permission is requested only where applicable to advertising. Manage permissions in system settings. Denial may prevent the relevant feature, but not unrelated features.

## 7. Retention and deletion
Local files and print records remain until you delete them or the system clears them. Uninstalling generally removes local app data, but exported files and existing backups may remain. Apple, Google and websites retain information under their own policies and legal duties; we cannot directly delete all records they independently control. If you email support, we process your address, message and attachments to respond and retain them only as needed for support and legal obligations. Avoid sending unnecessary sensitive information.

## 8. Disclosure and international processing
We do not sell document contents to advertisers. Requested printing, browsing, purchasing and support may transmit relevant information to printers, websites, Apple, Google or email providers. Providers may process data outside your country. We take measures required by applicable law and respect applicable consent and choices.

## 9. Security
We use system permissions, local storage and platform safeguards to reasonably protect information. No device, network or third-party service is absolutely secure. Protect access to your device and choose networks, printers and websites carefully.

## 10. Choices and rights
You can delete local files, manage permissions and subscriptions, and adjust advertising privacy choices where the app provides an entry. Depending on applicable law, you may have rights of access, correction, deletion, withdrawal of consent and objection. Contact us to exercise them; we may need to verify identity and scope. Withdrawal does not affect earlier lawful processing.

## 11. Minors
NetPrint is not specifically directed to children. Minors should use it with guardian guidance and obtain permission before purchasing. Contact us if you believe children’s personal information has been improperly processed.

## 12. Updates and contact
We may update this policy when features, providers or legal requirements change. We update the date, provide appropriate notice of material changes and seek renewed consent when legally required. For privacy questions or rights requests, contact SunnyStark at ycfiggy@gmail.com.
